<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26923" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lŏgĭcus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λογικός</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>logical,
				reasonable</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">haeresis medicorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Isid. 4, 4, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alia logica, alia aloga memorantur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 9, § 949</span></i>
			.—Hence, in <i>plur. subst.</i>,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lŏgĭca</span></b> ,
				ōrum, n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ λογικά</span>, <i>logic</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">habes ea, quae de perturbationibus enucleate
					disputant Stoici, quae logica appellant, quia disseruntur
					subtilius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Tusc. 4, 14, 33</span></i>
			.—In sing.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lŏgĭcum</span></b> ,
			i, n., <i>logic</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Sid. Carm. 15,
			100</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lŏgĭci</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>rational physicians</i>, <i><span class="en">Cael.
				Aur. Acut. 3, 21, 216</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
